#!/usr/bin/env python3.11
"""github-activity-capture — GitHub review verdicts, review comments,
conversation comments and the merged-PR changelog, captured as signals (E25,
issue_01M4ZB5C5ZX0MV206064MTRAE0), so Orient can retire its own GitHub
capture (convivy-orient's github_capture.py, which rides the operator's
personal `gh` login).

AUTHENTICATES AS THE INSTALL'S OWN GITHUB APP (`github_app.installed_app()`), never
`gh`, mirroring `bin/pr-state-capture` and `bin/ci-result-capture`. UNLIKE either
sibling, this job's tokens carry NO `issues` permission at all (operator's
ruling, 2026-10-15, relayed by the steward): work items live in the
Library's corrections queue, GitHub issues are not a Convivy surface, and
`issue_comment` is not one of this job's four kinds. `lib/agent-platform/
github_activity.py` holds the four kinds' transforms and the per-repository
read/post pass (`capture_repository`); this script is the launchd entry
point that walks every installation's repositories and calls it.

ONE INSTALLATION PER OWNER, READ FROM THE APP'S OWN INSTALLATION LIST, NOT
FROM THE PROJECT REGISTRY. `pr-state-capture.repos_to_capture()` derives
its repo list from the registry because Deck's PR-ladder panel needs every
registered repo covered even ones the App reaches only through a "selected
repositories" installation; this job instead asks each installation
directly which repositories it reaches (`list_installation_repos`, mirroring
`pr-state-capture.installed_repos` but keeping the full repo object, not
just its name) — a repo the App cannot read is never in that list, and
nothing here needs the registry to notice a 404 on it the way that sibling
does. `GA.installations` gives one entry per installation; a failure minting
one installation's token is logged and costs only that installation's
repos, not the whole pass.

EXCLUDED FROM EVERY PASS: an archived repository (`archived` on the
installation's own repo object); the two sandbox-tool repositories Orient's
job also excludes (`SANDBOX_REPOS`, named directly rather than derived,
mirroring how Orient's own job names them); and every repository of a BLACK
BOX project (`projects.private_slugs()`, platform/decisions/0043). THIS
THIRD EXCLUSION GOES BEYOND THE EPIC'S OWN TEXT (issue_01M4ZB5C5ZX0MV206064MTRAE0),
which names only "every non-archived repository ... except the sandbox-tool
repositories the job names." A private project's repository is never
registered with a product the Library's signal store recognises, and
`pr-state-capture.repos_to_capture()` already excludes private-project repos
from ITS OWN capture for the identical reason (ADR-0043's wall: none of a
black-box crew's content reaches a shared store). Without this exclusion, a
private-project repo's pull requests would 404 against the Library's
`POST /signals` every pass, and `capture_repository`'s own cursor rule holds
a repo's cursor exactly where it was whenever any post in that pass fails —
so every later pass would re-read and re-fail the same repository's full
window forever, never advancing past it.

A FOURTH EXCLUSION, ADDED IN SECURITY REVIEW ROUND 1 (CQ·605):
`GACT.is_safe_basename()` refuses a repository whose bare basename is not a
safe path/CLI segment (reuses `worktrees._is_safe_segment`, the guard
`is_dispatch_target` already applies to the identical pattern). The
installation listing, not the registry, names these repositories, so a
basename of `.` or `..` is reachable here; refusing it before
`capture_repository` ever runs keeps that value out of every signal's
`product`/`stream`, which `bin/changelog-drain` later reads as a path
segment and an `agentctl spawn --on` argument. `_capturable_repos()` is the
ONE place that applies this exclusion (and the archived/sandbox/
private-project ones above it): round 1 added the basename skip only to
`main()`'s loop, so `--audit-window` still read a refused repository's real
events, found no row for them (`main()` never posted one) and reported
every one a miss (review round 2 finding) — factored into this one helper
so `main()`'s posting loop and `run_audit()`'s read-only loop can no longer
drift apart on which repositories they skip.

REPO NAMES ARE NEVER ESCAPED BEFORE BUILDING A GITHUB URL. Every `repo`
string this script and `github_activity.py` interpolate into a GitHub API
URL comes from GitHub's own installation-repository listing (`full_name`)
— never from the project registry, user input or any other source — and
GitHub itself restricts a repository name to letters, digits, `.`, `-` and
`_`. No other path in this change builds a URL from a repo name reaching it
any other way, so no escaping or validation is added.

POSTING CREDENTIAL HAS NO SHARED-TOKEN FALLBACK, UNLIKE EITHER SIBLING.
`pr-state-capture.signal_token()`/`ci-result-capture.signal_token()` fall
back to `signal_client.token()` (the shared `agent-platform` credential)
with a one-time warning when their own token is absent. This job's absent
credential REFUSES THE WHOLE PASS instead, before any GitHub read
(`main()`'s credential check runs first): the shared token lacks the
`signal.create_review` capability all four of this job's kinds need to post
under, so posting under it would not degrade gracefully, it would 403 on
every `review_verdict`, `review_comment` and `pr_comment` (only `changelog`,
posted under `source: github`, would land) — a partial, silently-wrong
capture is worse than a loud refusal. `signal_token()` resolves
`GITHUB_ACTIVITY_CAPTURE_TOKEN` or the 0600 file
`~/.orient-control/github-activity-capture-token`.

ONE POSTING DEADLINE FOR THE WHOLE PASS (`_POST_DEADLINE_SECONDS`, 150s),
mirroring `pr-state-capture._RUN_DEADLINE_SECONDS`'s reasoning: this job's
own `StartInterval` is 180s, and a pass that runs long has its next
scheduled fire skipped rather than overlapping it (launchd.plist(5)), so
150s leaves headroom before the next firing instead of racing it.

A TRANSPORT ERROR (A RAW `OSError`: `urllib.error.URLError`, a socket
timeout, a connection reset, OR A TRUNCATED RESPONSE BODY — GitHub cutting
a page off mid-read, which `github_app.request` raises as a `ConnectionError`
chained from the underlying `http.client.IncompleteRead`) IS CAUGHT AT EVERY
GITHUB CALL `main()` MAKES, NOT ONLY INSIDE `capture_repository`.
`github_app.request` only catches `urllib.error.HTTPError`; any other
failure propagates as an `OSError` through every other call built on it,
which is exactly how `pr-state-capture` crashed on this machine: its own
`main` called `list_pulls` called `github_app.request`, a
`ConnectionResetError` reached nothing that caught it, and that pass ended
with every owner after the failing one never read (review round on #916).
This job makes the same four kinds of call and catches each at the cost it
can afford:

- `GA.installations`, before the per-owner loop, has no narrower scope to
  fall back to: the error is logged and `main()` returns 1.
- `GA.installation_token` and `list_installation_repos`, inside the loop,
  cost only their owner: logged as `<owner>: transport error ...`,
  `exit_code` set to 1, and the loop moves on to the next owner.
- the `GET /rate_limit` read is diagnostic only: its failure is logged on
  the existing "rate limit could not be read" line, naming the error
  type, and does not by itself set `exit_code`.
- `GACT.capture_repository`, per repository (the original catch, added in
  the review round on #910 that added `capture_repository`): logged, that
  repository's cursor is left exactly as it was, and the loop moves on to
  the next repository.

Usage:
    github-activity-capture
    github-activity-capture --audit-window START END

`--audit-window START END` (both ISO-8601 UTC, e.g. 2026-10-20T00:00:00Z) is a
READ-ONLY check (CQ·494, E25 PR 4) that every review verdict, merge, review
comment and conversation comment GitHub reports in [START, END] has landed in
the Library under THIS job's own posting credential — the proof the overlap
window needs before Orient's own GitHub capture can retire. It never posts
and never moves the cursor; it refuses on the same missing credential as an
ordinary pass. Exits 0 when every event matched, 1 when any did not (printing
one line per miss: kind, repo, the GitHub object's URL and why — no row, a
row ingested by another identity, or skipped by the same empty-body rule the
job itself applies) or the window itself is invalid (END not after START, or
longer than 7 days — this audit is for one overlap window, not a backfill).
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import datetime as dt
import json
import os
import sys
import time
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request
from pathlib import Path

sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / "lib" / "agent-platform"))

import github_activity as GACT  # noqa: E402
import github_app as GA  # noqa: E402
import projects  # noqa: E402
import signal_client as SC  # noqa: E402
import vault_plane as VP  # noqa: E402

# The install's own GitHub App (issue_01M2KV16ZRG3N49GRER8Q7545H), the same App
# `bin/pr-state-capture` and `bin/ci-result-capture` already authenticate as —
# resolved fresh per run through `GA.installed_app()`, never a literal, never stored.

# The token this script mints can only ever read pull requests (and their
# reviews/comments, which live under the same `pull_requests` scope) and the
# installation's own metadata — NO `issues` permission at all (see the
# module docstring). A bug that tried to write, or to read a GitHub issue,
# would be refused by GitHub itself.
_READ_ONLY_PERMISSIONS = {"pull_requests": "read", "metadata": "read"}

# This job's OWN POST /signals credential — see the module docstring's
# "POSTING CREDENTIAL HAS NO SHARED-TOKEN FALLBACK" section for why `main()`
# refuses the pass rather than falling back to the shared agent-platform
# token the way `pr-state-capture`/`ci-result-capture` do.
SIGNAL_TOKEN_ENV = "GITHUB_ACTIVITY_CAPTURE_TOKEN"
SIGNAL_TOKEN_FILE = Path.home() / ".orient-control" / "github-activity-capture-token"

# The same repositories Orient's own capture (convivy-orient's
# github_capture.py) excludes, per the epic's specification
# (issue_01M4ZB5C5ZX0MV206064MTRAE0) — named directly there rather than
# derived, and read here from each unit's own `activity_capture_excluded_repos`
# (projects.activity_capture_excluded_repos) rather than a second hardcoded
# copy. All under `convivy`, this job's primary owner.
SANDBOX_REPOS = {projects.repo_github_slug(r)
                 for r in projects.activity_capture_excluded_repos()}

# One deadline for the whole pass' signal posting, not per signal — see the
# module docstring's "ONE POSTING DEADLINE FOR THE WHOLE PASS" section.
_POST_DEADLINE_SECONDS = 150

_PAGE_SIZE = 100
# Bounds the installation-repository listing to 1000 repos per owner, so an
# unexpectedly large installation degrades to "this pass saw its first 1000"
# (loud, via GA.Unreadable) rather than an unbounded page loop.
_MAX_PAGES = 10


def signal_token() -> str | None:
    """`SIGNAL_TOKEN_ENV` or the 0600 file `SIGNAL_TOKEN_FILE`, or `None`
    when neither is set. Unlike `pr-state-capture.signal_token`/
    `ci-result-capture.signal_token`, a `None` here is never papered over
    with the shared agent-platform token — see the module docstring."""
    tok = os.environ.get(SIGNAL_TOKEN_ENV, "").strip()
    if tok:
        return tok
    try:
        return SIGNAL_TOKEN_FILE.read_text().strip() or None
    except OSError:
        return None


def private_repo_slugs() -> set[str]:
    """Lowercased `owner/repo` for every repository of a BLACK BOX project
    (`projects.private_slugs()`, platform/decisions/0043) — see the module
    docstring's "EXCLUDED FROM EVERY PASS" section for why this job excludes
    them, beyond what the epic's own text names."""
    private = projects.private_slugs()
    return {projects.repo_github_slug(r, unit).lower()
           for slug, unit in projects.load().items() if slug in private
           for r in unit.get("repos", [])}


def list_installation_repos(token: str, *, opener=urllib.request.urlopen) -> list[dict]:
    """Every repository object the installation reaches — GitHub's own repo
    object (carrying `full_name` and `archived`), not just a name, so
    `archived` can be read off it directly rather than refetched per repo.
    Mirrors `pr-state-capture.installed_repos`'s paging, but keeps the whole
    object instead of reducing it to a lowercased name set."""
    out: list[dict] = []
    for page in range(1, _MAX_PAGES + 1):
        code, payload = GA.request(
            "GET", f"{GA.API}/installation/repositories?per_page={_PAGE_SIZE}&page={page}",
            token, None, opener=opener)
        repos = payload.get("repositories") if isinstance(payload, dict) else None
        if code != 200 or not isinstance(repos, list):
            raise GA.Unreadable(f"the installation's repositories could not be read ({code})")
        out.extend(repos)
        if len(repos) < _PAGE_SIZE:
            return out
    raise GA.Unreadable(f"the installation lists more than {_MAX_PAGES * _PAGE_SIZE} "
                        f"repositories; refusing to treat an unread page as absence")


def _capturable_repos(repos: list[dict], excluded: set[str]) -> list[str]:
    """Every `repo_obj["full_name"]` in `repos`, sorted, after the one filter
    `main()`'s posting loop and `run_audit()`'s read-only loop must both
    apply: missing name, archived, excluded (sandbox/private-project,
    case-insensitive) or an unsafe basename (`GACT.is_safe_basename`, round 1,
    CQ·605) — one definition so the two loops cannot drift the way they did
    in round 1: `run_audit()` had no basename skip, so a repository `main()`
    refused and never posted a signal for still had its real events read
    back and reported as misses (round 2 finding, CQ·605). Prints the same
    refusal line for an unsafe basename either loop would have printed on
    its own."""
    out: list[str] = []
    for repo_obj in sorted(repos, key=lambda r: (r.get("full_name") or "").lower()):
        full_name = repo_obj.get("full_name") or ""
        if not full_name or repo_obj.get("archived") or full_name.lower() in excluded:
            continue
        if not GACT.is_safe_basename(full_name):
            # The installation listing, not the reviewed project registry
            # (see the module docstring's "ONE INSTALLATION PER OWNER"
            # section) — refused here, before any signal or audit read ever
            # carries this basename as product/stream, so nothing
            # downstream (bin/changelog-drain's path check and
            # `agentctl spawn --on`) ever sees it (security review round 1,
            # CQ·605).
            print(f"github-activity-capture: refusing repository with an "
                 f"unsafe basename: {full_name!r}", file=sys.stderr)
            continue
        out.append(full_name)
    return out


def _require_signal_token() -> str | None:
    """This job's own posting credential, or `None` after printing the
    refusal `main()` and `run_audit()` both act on — see the module
    docstring's "POSTING CREDENTIAL HAS NO SHARED-TOKEN FALLBACK" section.
    One definition so the audit refuses on exactly the same missing
    credential, with the same message, as an ordinary pass."""
    tok = signal_token()
    if not tok:
        print(f"github-activity-capture: no {SIGNAL_TOKEN_FILE} and no "
             f"${SIGNAL_TOKEN_ENV}; refusing to read GitHub without this "
             f"job's own posting credential (no fallback to the shared "
             f"agent-platform token: it lacks the signal.create_review "
             f"capability this job's kinds need)", file=sys.stderr)
        return None
    return tok


def _app_auth() -> str | None:
    """A fresh App JWT, or `None` after printing why it could not be
    minted. Shared by `main()` and `run_audit()` so both refuse on the
    same key problem with the same message."""
    try:
        app = GA.installed_app()
    except GA.Unreadable as e:
        print(f"github-activity-capture: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return None
    problem = GA.key_problem(app.key_path, label="the install's GitHub App")
    if problem:
        print(f"github-activity-capture: {problem}", file=sys.stderr)
        return None
    try:
        return GA.app_jwt(app.key_path, app.app_id)
    except GA.Unreadable as e:
        print(f"github-activity-capture: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return None


# --- audit: a read-only check that every window event landed under this
#     job's own credential (CQ·494, E25 PR 4) ---------------------------------
#
# Why this exists and what it must never do: see the module docstring's
# `--audit-window` section. It never calls `SC.post_signal` (or anything
# that does) and never touches `GACT.load_cursor`/`save_cursor`.

# One overlap window, not a backfill — the epic's own 24-hour pause is the
# case this is sized for; a caller asking for more is almost certainly
# naming the wrong window rather than meaning it.
_AUDIT_WINDOW_MAX = dt.timedelta(days=7)

# The four kinds `github_activity.py`'s transforms produce — see that
# module's docstring. `issue_comment` is deliberately not one of them (the
# operator's ruling the module docstring records), so it is never audited.
_AUDIT_KINDS = ("review_verdict", "changelog", "review_comment", "pr_comment")

# `GET /signals`' own page cap (library-protocol §3), mirrored here the same
# way `bin/mcp-ops-server`'s `SIGNAL_LIST_MAX` is.
_SIGNAL_PAGE_LIMIT = 200
# Bounds a single (repo, kind) read-back the same way `_MAX_PAGES` bounds an
# installation's repository listing: a loud refusal past this many pages,
# never a silent partial read treated as the whole answer.
_MAX_SIGNAL_PAGES = 50


class AuditError(RuntimeError):
    """A window, credential or Library-identity problem the audit cannot
    recover from — distinct from a per-event miss, which is printed and
    counted rather than raised."""


def _parse_audit_bound(raw: str, name: str) -> dt.datetime:
    """`raw` as a UTC-zoned `datetime`, or raises `AuditError` naming `name`
    (`"START"`/`"END"`) when it is not ISO-8601 or carries no zone — the
    same "Z" shape GitHub's own timestamps use (`github_activity._parse_ts`),
    required explicitly here because an unzoned string parsed as local time
    would silently shift the window by the host's offset."""
    try:
        value = dt.datetime.fromisoformat(raw.replace("Z", "+00:00"))
    except ValueError:
        raise AuditError(f"{name} {raw!r} is not an ISO-8601 timestamp") from None
    if value.tzinfo is None:
        raise AuditError(f"{name} {raw!r} carries no UTC zone (e.g. "
                         f"2026-10-20T00:00:00Z)")
    return value.astimezone(dt.timezone.utc)


def whoami(token: str, *, opener=urllib.request.urlopen) -> str:
    """This credential's own `actor`, exactly as the Library's `GET /whoami`
    resolves it (library-protocol §2: "`GET /whoami` returns the calling
    identity as the Library resolved it ... so a client can assert on what
    it holds instead of assuming it"). This is the identity a `GET /signals`
    row's `ingested_by` carries when THIS credential is the one that posted
    it — the one way the audit can tell its own rows apart from Orient's or
    anyone else's without posting anything itself. `GET /whoami` has no
    Orient counterpart, so this reaches the Library's own address
    (`vault_plane.library_url`) rather than the translated, plane-aware one
    `SC.post_signal` uses. Raises `AuditError` on any transport failure, non-
    200 or missing `actor`: the audit cannot tell a miss from a mismatch
    without first knowing its own identity, so a degraded "unknown" identity
    here must never read as a clean pass."""
    req = urllib.request.Request(VP.library_url("/whoami"),
                                 headers=VP.library_headers(token=token))
    try:
        with opener(req, timeout=SC._DELIVERY_TIMEOUT) as resp:
            payload = json.loads(resp.read().decode("utf-8"))
    except Exception as e:
        raise AuditError(f"GET /whoami failed: {type(e).__name__}: {e}") from e
    actor = payload.get("actor") if isinstance(payload, dict) else None
    if not actor:
        raise AuditError(f"GET /whoami returned no actor: {payload!r:.200}")
    return actor


def _read_ingested_urls(repo: str, kind: str, since_iso: str, token: str, *,
                        opener=urllib.request.urlopen) -> dict[str, str | None]:
    """Every `refs.url` -> `ingested_by` the Library holds for `kind` and
    `product=` `repo`'s bare basename (CQ·605 — every signal writer's
    `product` is the bare repo name, never `owner/repo`), with
    `produced_at` on or after `since_iso` (library-protocol §3.2's `GET
    /signals` filters) — paged to the end via `offset`/`truncated` the way
    `issue_client.list_ledger_entries` pages. `dedup_key` is never served
    (library-protocol §3.1), which is why the audit matches on `refs.url`
    instead: see the module docstring. A row with no `refs.url` is skipped
    — nothing `github_activity.py`'s own transforms ever produce lacks one,
    so a row without one did not come from this job's own posting path
    either. Raises `AuditError` on any transport failure, non-200 or
    missing `signals` list."""
    product = GACT._repo_basename(repo)
    out: dict[str, str | None] = {}
    offset = 0
    for _ in range(_MAX_SIGNAL_PAGES):
        qs = urllib.parse.urlencode({"kind": kind, "product": product, "since": since_iso,
                                     "limit": _SIGNAL_PAGE_LIMIT, "offset": offset})
        req = urllib.request.Request(VP.url(f"/api/signals?{qs}"),
                                     headers=VP.headers(token=token))
        try:
            with opener(req, timeout=SC._DELIVERY_TIMEOUT) as resp:
                payload = json.loads(resp.read().decode("utf-8"))
        except Exception as e:
            raise AuditError(f"GET /signals (kind={kind}, product={product}) failed: "
                             f"{type(e).__name__}: {e}") from e
        rows = payload.get("signals") if isinstance(payload, dict) else None
        if not isinstance(rows, list):
            raise AuditError(f"GET /signals (kind={kind}, product={product}) returned "
                             f"no signals list: {payload!r:.200}")
        for row in rows:
            url = (row.get("refs") or {}).get("url") if isinstance(row, dict) else None
            if url:
                out[url] = row.get("ingested_by")
        if not payload.get("truncated") or not rows:
            return out
        offset += len(rows)
    raise AuditError(f"GET /signals (kind={kind}, product={product}) still truncated "
                     f"after {_MAX_SIGNAL_PAGES} pages; refusing to keep paging")


def _collect_window_events(repo: str, start: dt.datetime, end: dt.datetime, token: str, *,
                           opener=urllib.request.urlopen,
                           sleep=time.sleep) -> list[tuple[str, str, dict | None]]:
    """Every GitHub event of the four kinds in `[start, end]`, as `(kind,
    github_url, signal_or_none)` — `github_url` is the raw object's own
    `html_url`, always present even when the transform returns `None`
    (the empty-body skip), because a miss line needs a URL regardless of
    which of the three reasons it carries. Reviews are matched by
    `submitted_at`, merges by `merged_at`, both kinds of comment by
    `created_at`, per the plan this audit was built from. Reuses PR 2's own
    fetchers and transforms (`github_activity.py`) — no second copy of
    either."""
    since_iso = GACT._format_ts(start)
    events: list[tuple[str, str, dict | None]] = []

    for rc in GACT.fetch_review_comments(repo, since_iso, token, opener=opener, sleep=sleep):
        created = rc.get("created_at")
        if created and start <= GACT._parse_ts(created) <= end:
            events.append(("review_comment", rc.get("html_url") or "",
                          GACT.signal_from_review_comment(repo, rc)))

    for ic in GACT.fetch_conversation_comments(repo, since_iso, token, opener=opener,
                                               sleep=sleep):
        created = ic.get("created_at")
        if created and start <= GACT._parse_ts(created) <= end:
            events.append(("pr_comment", ic.get("html_url") or "",
                          GACT.signal_from_issue_comment(repo, ic)))

    prs = GACT.fetch_updated_pull_requests(repo, since_iso, token, opener=opener, sleep=sleep)
    for pr in prs:
        merged_at = pr.get("merged_at")
        if merged_at and start <= GACT._parse_ts(merged_at) <= end:
            events.append(("changelog", pr.get("html_url") or "",
                          GACT.signal_from_merge(repo, pr)))
        number = pr.get("number")
        for review in GACT.fetch_reviews(repo, number, token, opener=opener, sleep=sleep):
            submitted = review.get("submitted_at")
            if submitted and start <= GACT._parse_ts(submitted) <= end:
                events.append(("review_verdict", review.get("html_url") or "",
                              GACT.signal_from_review(repo, number, review)))
    return events


def _classify_window_events(repo: str, events: list[tuple[str, str, dict | None]],
                            start: dt.datetime, signal_tok: str, identity: str, *,
                            opener=urllib.request.urlopen) -> list[dict]:
    """Every event in `events`, matched (or not) against the Library's own
    rows — one `_read_ingested_urls` read per kind actually seen, not per
    event. Returns one dict per event: `{"repo", "kind", "url", "status",
    "reason"}`, `status` either `"matched"` or `"miss"`. The three miss
    reasons are the plan's own: no row at all, a row ingested by a
    different identity (Orient's, most likely, during the overlap window),
    or the same empty-body rule `github_activity.py`'s transforms apply —
    `events` already carries that decision as a `None` signal, classified
    here rather than re-derived."""
    since_iso = GACT._format_ts(start)
    ingested_by_kind: dict[str, dict[str, str | None]] = {}
    results: list[dict] = []
    for kind, url, sig in events:
        if sig is None:
            results.append({"repo": repo, "kind": kind, "url": url, "status": "miss",
                           "reason": "skipped by the empty-body rule"})
            continue
        match_url = sig["refs"]["url"]
        if kind not in ingested_by_kind:
            ingested_by_kind[kind] = _read_ingested_urls(repo, kind, since_iso, signal_tok,
                                                          opener=opener)
        if match_url not in ingested_by_kind[kind]:
            results.append({"repo": repo, "kind": kind, "url": match_url, "status": "miss",
                           "reason": "no row"})
            continue
        ingested_by = ingested_by_kind[kind][match_url]
        if ingested_by != identity:
            results.append({
                "repo": repo, "kind": kind, "url": match_url, "status": "miss",
                "reason": f"row ingested by {ingested_by!r}, not this job's own "
                         f"credential ({identity!r})"})
            continue
        results.append({"repo": repo, "kind": kind, "url": match_url, "status": "matched"})
    return results


def run_audit(start_raw: str, end_raw: str, *, opener=urllib.request.urlopen) -> int:
    """`--audit-window START END` — see the module docstring. Read-only:
    never posts, never moves the cursor. Returns 0 when every window event
    matched, 1 on any miss (printed as it is found) or an invalid window,
    credential or Library-identity problem (printed, then refused)."""
    sig_tok = _require_signal_token()
    if not sig_tok:
        return 1

    try:
        start = _parse_audit_bound(start_raw, "START")
        end = _parse_audit_bound(end_raw, "END")
    except AuditError as e:
        print(f"github-activity-capture: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    if end <= start:
        print(f"github-activity-capture: END ({end_raw!r}) must be after "
             f"START ({start_raw!r})", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    if end - start > _AUDIT_WINDOW_MAX:
        print(f"github-activity-capture: the window ({end - start}) exceeds "
             f"{_AUDIT_WINDOW_MAX}; this audit is for one overlap window, not "
             f"a backfill", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1

    jwt = _app_auth()
    if not jwt:
        return 1

    try:
        identity = whoami(sig_tok, opener=opener)
    except AuditError as e:
        print(f"github-activity-capture: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1

    try:
        installations = GA.installations(jwt, opener=opener)
    except (GA.Unreadable, OSError) as e:
        print(f"github-activity-capture: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1

    excluded = private_repo_slugs() | SANDBOX_REPOS
    tallies = {kind: {"matched": 0, "missed": 0} for kind in _AUDIT_KINDS}
    exit_code = 0

    for inst in sorted(installations,
                       key=lambda i: ((i.get("account") or {}).get("login") or "")):
        owner = ((inst.get("account") or {}).get("login")) or "?"
        inst_id = str(inst.get("id") or "")
        try:
            if not inst_id:
                raise GA.Unreadable("the installation carries no id")
            token = GA.installation_token(jwt, inst_id, permissions=_READ_ONLY_PERMISSIONS,
                                          opener=opener)
            repos = list_installation_repos(token, opener=opener)
        except (GA.Unreadable, OSError) as e:
            print(f"github-activity-capture: {owner}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
            exit_code = 1
            continue

        for full_name in _capturable_repos(repos, excluded):
            try:
                events = _collect_window_events(full_name, start, end, token, opener=opener)
                results = _classify_window_events(full_name, events, start, sig_tok, identity,
                                                   opener=opener)
            except (GACT.FetchError, AuditError, OSError) as e:
                print(f"github-activity-capture: {full_name}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
                exit_code = 1
                continue
            for r in results:
                if r["status"] == "matched":
                    tallies[r["kind"]]["matched"] += 1
                else:
                    tallies[r["kind"]]["missed"] += 1
                    exit_code = 1
                    print(f"github-activity-capture: miss kind={r['kind']} "
                         f"repo={r['repo']} url={r['url']!r} reason={r['reason']}")

    for kind in _AUDIT_KINDS:
        t = tallies[kind]
        print(f"github-activity-capture: audit {kind} matched={t['matched']} "
             f"missed={t['missed']}")
    return exit_code


def main() -> int:
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        description="Capture GitHub review verdicts, review comments, "
                    "conversation comments and the merged-PR changelog as "
                    "signals, authenticating as the install's own GitHub App.")
    parser.add_argument(
        "--audit-window", nargs=2, metavar=("START", "END"), default=None,
        help="read-only: audit that every GitHub event of the four kinds in "
            "[START, END] (ISO-8601 UTC) has a Library row ingested by this "
            "job's own credential — never posts, never moves the cursor; "
            "see the module docstring.")
    args = parser.parse_args()

    if args.audit_window is not None:
        return run_audit(*args.audit_window)

    pass_start_monotonic = time.monotonic()
    pass_start_wall = dt.datetime.now(dt.timezone.utc)

    # Checked BEFORE any GitHub read — see the module docstring's "POSTING
    # CREDENTIAL HAS NO SHARED-TOKEN FALLBACK" section.
    sig_tok = _require_signal_token()
    if not sig_tok:
        return 1

    jwt = _app_auth()
    if not jwt:
        return 1

    # Counts every GitHub request this pass makes, across every installation
    # and every repository — logged in the per-pass summary line below.
    request_count = [0]

    def counting_opener(req, timeout=None):
        request_count[0] += 1
        return urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout)

    try:
        installations = GA.installations(jwt, opener=counting_opener)
    except GA.Unreadable as e:
        print(f"github-activity-capture: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    except OSError as e:
        print(f"github-activity-capture: transport error reading the App's "
             f"installations: {type(e).__name__}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1

    excluded = private_repo_slugs() | SANDBOX_REPOS
    cursor = GACT.load_cursor()
    # Shared across every post this pass makes — see the module docstring's
    # "ONE POSTING DEADLINE FOR THE WHOLE PASS" section.
    post_deadline = time.monotonic() + _POST_DEADLINE_SECONDS

    def poster(payload: dict) -> str:
        return SC.post_signal(payload, tok=sig_tok, timeout=SC._DELIVERY_TIMEOUT,
                              deadline=post_deadline)

    exit_code = 0
    for inst in sorted(installations,
                       key=lambda i: ((i.get("account") or {}).get("login") or "")):
        owner = ((inst.get("account") or {}).get("login")) or "?"
        inst_id = str(inst.get("id") or "")
        try:
            if not inst_id:
                raise GA.Unreadable("the installation carries no id")
            token = GA.installation_token(jwt, inst_id, permissions=_READ_ONLY_PERMISSIONS,
                                          opener=counting_opener)
        except GA.Unreadable as e:
            print(f"github-activity-capture: {owner}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
            exit_code = 1
            continue
        except OSError as e:
            print(f"github-activity-capture: {owner}: transport error minting "
                 f"an installation token: {type(e).__name__}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
            exit_code = 1
            continue

        try:
            repos = list_installation_repos(token, opener=counting_opener)
        except GA.Unreadable as e:
            print(f"github-activity-capture: {owner}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
            exit_code = 1
            continue
        except OSError as e:
            print(f"github-activity-capture: {owner}: transport error listing "
                 f"the installation's repositories: {type(e).__name__}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
            exit_code = 1
            continue

        # GET /rate_limit does not itself count against the installation's
        # own rate limit (GitHub's documented behaviour) — read once per
        # owner so the DoD's hour-long sample has a per-owner trace in the
        # job's own log. Diagnostic only: a transport error here costs
        # nothing but this one log line — see the module docstring's "A
        # TRANSPORT ERROR ... IS CAUGHT" section.
        try:
            rate_code, rate_payload = GA.request("GET", f"{GA.API}/rate_limit", token, None,
                                                 opener=counting_opener)
        except OSError as e:
            print(f"github-activity-capture: {owner}: rate limit could not be "
                 f"read (transport error: {type(e).__name__}: {e})", file=sys.stderr)
        else:
            core = ((rate_payload.get("resources") or {}).get("core")
                   if rate_code == 200 and isinstance(rate_payload, dict) else None)
            if isinstance(core, dict):
                print(f"github-activity-capture: {owner}: core.used={core.get('used')} "
                     f"core.limit={core.get('limit')}")
            else:
                print(f"github-activity-capture: {owner}: rate limit could not be "
                     f"read ({rate_code})", file=sys.stderr)

        for full_name in _capturable_repos(repos, excluded):
            try:
                result = GACT.capture_repository(
                    full_name, cursor.get(full_name), token, poster, pass_start_wall,
                    opener=counting_opener)
            except OSError as e:
                # See the module docstring's "A TRANSPORT ERROR ... IS
                # CAUGHT HERE" section: this repo's cursor is left exactly
                # where it was (never written below), the next repository
                # still gets its turn, and the pass is marked failed.
                print(f"github-activity-capture: {full_name}: transport error "
                     f"reading GitHub: {type(e).__name__}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
                exit_code = 1
                continue
            # Saved after every repository, not once at the end of the pass:
            # a deadline or a crash partway through still keeps every
            # already-finished repository's cursor advance.
            cursor[full_name] = result["new_cursor"]
            GACT.save_cursor(cursor)
            if not result["may_advance"]:
                exit_code = 1

    pass_end_wall = dt.datetime.now(dt.timezone.utc)
    elapsed = time.monotonic() - pass_start_monotonic
    print(f"github-activity-capture: pass start={pass_start_wall.isoformat()} "
         f"end={pass_end_wall.isoformat()} elapsed={elapsed:.1f}s "
         f"requests={request_count[0]}")

    return exit_code


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
